# Measuring Detection Coverage

Organizations should periodically review their ATT&CK coverage.

Example questions include:

- Which tactics are monitored?
- Which techniques lack detections?
- Which detections produce frequent false positives?
- Which techniques are highest priority based on organizational risk?

Coverage reviews help prioritize future engineering efforts.

---

# Best Practices

When using ATT&CK:

- Map detections only to techniques supported by evidence.
- Review mappings as detections evolve.
- Use sub-techniques when appropriate.
- Align threat hunting with ATT&CK tactics.
- Measure coverage regularly.
- Avoid assigning techniques based on assumptions.

---

# Common Challenges

Security teams often encounter:

- Incorrect ATT&CK mappings.
- Overly broad technique assignments.
- Failure to update mappings.
- Inconsistent use across teams.
- Treating ATT&CK as a checklist rather than an analytical framework.

Regular reviews improve consistency and accuracy.

